WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.664
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Cambridge exams.

2
00:00:05.964 --> 00:00:09.443
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.743 --> 00:00:19.094
Unit twenty: C1 Advanced: Speaking and Exam Strategy. Today you will speak fluently, evaluate ideas with a partner and plan for exam day.

4
00:00:19.394 --> 00:00:22.081
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:23.033 --> 00:00:26.231
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:27.083 --> 00:00:28.119
Fluency.

7
00:00:29.117 --> 00:00:31.209
Fluency means speaking smoothly.

8
00:00:31.817 --> 00:00:33.491
Fluency is assessed.

9
00:00:34.083 --> 00:00:36.701
Your turn. Say: Fluency.

10
00:00:39.567 --> 00:00:40.545
Fluency.

11
00:00:41.283 --> 00:00:42.354
Evaluate.

12
00:00:43.350 --> 00:00:46.232
Evaluate means to judge the value of something.

13
00:00:46.817 --> 00:00:48.468
Evaluate the options.

14
00:00:49.083 --> 00:00:51.840
Your turn. Say: Evaluate.

15
00:00:54.700 --> 00:00:55.748
Evaluate.

16
00:00:56.483 --> 00:00:57.589
Speculate.

17
00:00:58.583 --> 00:01:01.256
Speculate means to guess about possibilities.

18
00:01:01.850 --> 00:01:03.501
Speculate about the photo.

19
00:01:04.117 --> 00:01:06.688
Your turn. Say: Speculate.

20
00:01:09.533 --> 00:01:10.697
Speculate.

21
00:01:11.450 --> 00:01:12.544
Collaborate.

22
00:01:13.550 --> 00:01:15.608
Collaborate means to work together.

23
00:01:16.217 --> 00:01:17.914
Collaborate with your partner.

24
00:01:18.517 --> 00:01:21.146
Your turn. Say: Collaborate.

25
00:01:24.000 --> 00:01:24.955
Collaborate.

26
00:01:25.717 --> 00:01:26.520
Hedge.

27
00:01:27.517 --> 00:01:30.712
Hedge means to speak cautiously with words like perhaps.

28
00:01:31.317 --> 00:01:32.840
Use hedging language.

29
00:01:33.450 --> 00:01:35.742
Your turn. Say: Hedge.

30
00:01:38.600 --> 00:01:39.311
Hedge.

31
00:01:40.050 --> 00:01:40.981
Interrupt.

32
00:01:41.983 --> 00:01:44.343
Interrupt means to stop someone speaking.

33
00:01:44.950 --> 00:01:46.636
Do not interrupt your partner.

34
00:01:47.250 --> 00:01:49.775
Your turn. Say: Interrupt.

35
00:01:52.633 --> 00:01:53.530
Interrupt.

36
00:01:54.283 --> 00:01:55.668
Discourse marker.

37
00:01:56.683 --> 00:01:59.519
Discourse marker means a word like well or in fact.

38
00:02:00.117 --> 00:02:01.826
Use discourse markers.

39
00:02:02.417 --> 00:02:05.290
Your turn. Say: Discourse marker.

40
00:02:08.133 --> 00:02:09.564
Discourse marker.

41
00:02:10.317 --> 00:02:11.306
Strategy.

42
00:02:12.317 --> 00:02:14.711
Strategy means a plan to reach a goal.

43
00:02:15.317 --> 00:02:17.165
Have a strategy for each paper.

44
00:02:17.750 --> 00:02:20.449
Your turn. Say: Strategy.

45
00:02:23.300 --> 00:02:24.406
Strategy.

46
00:02:25.200 --> 00:02:29.164
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:30.017 --> 00:02:32.190
Visal, what is in C1 Speaking?

48
00:02:33.283 --> 00:02:45.827
There are four parts: an interview, a long turn comparing photos, a collaborative task and a discussion. You speak for about fifteen minutes with a partner and two examiners.

49
00:02:46.917 --> 00:02:48.730
How can I speak at C1?

50
00:02:49.817 --> 00:03:03.197
Speculate and evaluate with phrases such as it might be that or the most convincing reason is. Use discourse markers and hedging, and invite your partner to speak.

51
00:03:04.283 --> 00:03:06.353
What is the best exam strategy?

52
00:03:07.450 --> 00:03:20.911
Plan your time on every paper, check instructions and always finish. In the final week take full timed practice tests, review feedback and rest well before the exam.

53
00:03:22.067 --> 00:03:23.497
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:24.350 --> 00:03:27.093
Grammar focus: Strategy: speculate, evaluate, collaborate.

55
00:03:27.393 --> 00:03:28.533
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:29.217 --> 00:03:32.029
It might be that the people are preparing for a festival.

57
00:03:32.917 --> 00:03:35.964
What do you think? I'd be interested to hear your view.

58
00:03:36.900 --> 00:03:45.566
Speak naturally, speculate and evaluate with precise language, and collaborate with your partner. Plan every paper and practise under timed conditions.

59
00:03:46.317 --> 00:03:50.153
Be careful! Don't say: I interrupt my partner.

60
00:03:52.100 --> 00:03:54.924
Say: I invite my partner to speak.

61
00:03:55.224 --> 00:03:56.237
Collaborate.

62
00:03:57.033 --> 00:03:59.825
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

63
00:04:00.633 --> 00:04:01.727
Exam Week.

64
00:04:02.027 --> 00:04:05.107
Vireak takes timed practice tests in the last week.

65
00:04:06.100 --> 00:04:10.514
In Speaking practice he speculates about a photo and evaluates ideas.

66
00:04:11.500 --> 00:04:14.440
He invites his partner to speak with a short question.

67
00:04:15.433 --> 00:04:18.246
He reviews feedback from his teacher every evening.

68
00:04:19.233 --> 00:04:22.974
On the day before the exam he rests and prepares his documents.

69
00:04:24.067 --> 00:04:28.428
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

70
00:04:29.283 --> 00:04:32.154
C1 Speaking lasts about blank minutes.

71
00:04:32.454 --> 00:04:36.026
A, two. B, sixty. C, fifteen.

72
00:04:39.567 --> 00:04:41.915
The answer is C: fifteen.

73
00:04:43.050 --> 00:04:44.608
To speculate is to blank.

74
00:04:44.908 --> 00:04:49.224
A, guess about possibilities. B, finish. C, copy.

75
00:04:52.767 --> 00:04:55.869
The answer is A: guess about possibilities.

76
00:04:57.017 --> 00:04:58.598
You should blank your partner.

77
00:04:58.898 --> 00:05:02.180
A, ignore. B, invite. C, interrupt.

78
00:05:05.733 --> 00:05:07.594
The answer is B: invite.

79
00:05:08.750 --> 00:05:10.459
Before the exam you should blank.

80
00:05:10.759 --> 00:05:15.156
A, study all night. B, skip sleep. C, rest.

81
00:05:18.700 --> 00:05:20.409
The answer is C: rest.

82
00:05:21.550 --> 00:05:23.712
Vireak uses feedback to blank.

83
00:05:24.012 --> 00:05:27.979
A, improve. B, ignore. C, hide mistakes.

84
00:05:31.533 --> 00:05:33.614
The answer is A: improve.

85
00:05:34.800 --> 00:05:37.789
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

86
00:05:38.650 --> 00:05:41.311
How do you prepare for the C1 Advanced exam?

87
00:05:50.117 --> 00:05:51.582
Now listen to Visal.

88
00:05:51.882 --> 00:06:07.900
I take full timed practice tests and review each mistake. In Speaking I practise speculating and evaluating ideas with a partner. In the last week I rest well and check that I know the plan for each paper.

89
00:06:08.200 --> 00:06:09.735
Excellent answer, Visal!

90
00:06:10.650 --> 00:06:16.623
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and strategy: speculate, evaluate, collaborate.

91
00:06:16.923 --> 00:06:22.176
Today's value is self-discipline. Control your habits, so your habits do not control you.

92
00:06:22.476 --> 00:06:28.846
Congratulations! You have finished Online Cambridge exams. See you in Online Grade nine English!

93
00:06:29.146 --> 00:06:31.787
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

